nrsc5-studio (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AGC: amplitude-first pre-stage. New SearchPhase::AmpProbe runs
    ahead of the MER coarse/fine controller, binary-searching the
    device gain table against an RMS-dBFS target (per-profile:
    -20 dBFS for RTL-SDR, -22 dBFS for SDRplay), then hands off
    to the existing MER hill-climb seeded at the amplitude
    bracket. Bounds the initial gain choice in <1 s on cold-start
    tunes; cache hits skip AmpProbe entirely. Settings -> Gain
    grew an "Advanced AGC tuning" section with a slider to
    override the per-profile target for unusual antennas /
    preamps.
  * libnrsc5 bumped from v3.1.0 to v3.2.0. Picks up FFTW
    input/output alignment (perf bump in the synchronizer FFT)
    and an audio output queue refactor for free. Four new
    libnrsc5 events are wired through:
      - EXCITER_INFO / IMPORTER_INFO -> "Equipment" block in
        Station Info (manufacturer ID, core + manufacturer
        firmware version, importer-connected flag).
      - LOCAL_TIME -> "Time" block in Station Info (broadcaster
        UTC offset, DST regional/local flags, DST schedule).
      - LEAP_SECOND_OFFSET -> GPS-UTC offset row with hover
        tooltip for pending leap-second adjustments.
  * Packaging: stop shipping install-nrsc5-helper.sh from
    /usr/share/nrsc5-studio/. v0.5.1's changelog claimed this
    was done, but the script was still installed by debian/rules
    and the lintian-overrides + AppStream metainfo still
    referenced it. v0.6.0 finishes the cleanup.

 -- LTCAshraven <ltcashraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0000

nrsc5-studio (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Decode pipeline now runs ONE libnrsc5 session per station tuned.
    The single `nrsc5_pipe_samples_cu8` session demuxes every
    advertised HD subchannel internally and emits per-program PCM
    via the audio callback's `program` field, so the v0.5.0 design
    (one feeder + one session per HD1-HD4 toggle) was running the
    same decode work up to four times in parallel against the same
    I/Q. Thanks to argilo (upstream nrsc5 maintainer) for the
    review.
  * GUI: HD1-HD4 buttons no longer have per-program on/off toggles.
    Every advertised subchannel decodes automatically and the row
    just picks the speaker program. Auto-decode and max-concurrent
    settings are gone (no longer meaningful).
  * Keyboard shortcuts simplified: Alt+1..Alt+8 selects the speaker
    program. The old Ctrl+Alt+1..Ctrl+Alt+8 / Ctrl+Alt+X shortcuts
    are removed.
  * Packaging: drop the `nrsc5` helper (Recommends + post-install
    script). v0.5.0 moved decode in-process via libnrsc5; the
    external `nrsc5` CLI is no longer used at runtime.

 -- LTCAshraven <ltcashraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

nrsc5-studio (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libnrsc5 in-process cutover. nrsc5.exe is gone from bin/; the
    decoder is now linked dynamically against libnrsc5.dll /
    libnrsc5.so and runs as a thread inside the app. New FFI layer
    under src/ffi/ (raw bindings + safe wrapper + per-program
    DecoderInstance). 100% of the project's unsafe code is now
    isolated to src/ffi/api.rs.
  * Multi-program HD decode. A single SDR tune now feeds up to 4
    HD subchannels (HD1-HD4) in parallel via a shared IqBus fan-out.
    Central AGC tee, per-program play_log dedup, soft cap of 4
    active decoders.
  * Fix Linux rtl_tcp GUI freeze on Start. Hostname resolution +
    bounded connect (3s) + bounded handshake read (2s) so a bad
    host or wrong port fails in ~5s instead of locking the GUI
    until the OS produces a Force-Quit dialog.
  * Ship res/map.png in the .deb/.rpm install at
    /usr/share/nrsc5-studio/res/map.png so the weather overlay's
    fallback base map is available on Linux. The maps module now
    searches FHS install paths in addition to the portable res/
    directory.
  * License: the shipped binary is now a GPL-3.0 combined work
    (the Rust source is still MIT). Ship COPYING.GPL-3.0 at
    /usr/share/doc/nrsc5-studio/COPYING.GPL-3.0. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
    rewritten to document the GPL-2.0/2.1+ libraries statically
    embedded inside libnrsc5.dll (FFTW3, FAAD2, libusb 1.0.27,
    rtl-sdr 2.0.2).
  * Smaller fixes: LOT filename prefix no longer doubled; MER
    resets to zero on retune; Enter key inside the Tuner frequency
    field triggers tune; cargo-gnu.ps1 prepends MSYS2 mingw64 to
    PATH so the right pkg-config and libclang are picked.

 -- LTCAshraven <ltcashraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 02 Jun 2026 14:14:01 +0000

nrsc5-studio (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SDR transport refactor. The [sdr] config models the data source
    as an explicit `transport` field (LocalSoapy / SoapyRemote /
    rtl_tcp). The pre-0.3.0 USB-direct and pre-0.5.0 `nrsc5 -H`
    start paths are gone — every Start goes through the in-process
    piped IQ → spectrum → AGC → nrsc5 pipeline regardless of
    transport. Legacy `use_rtl_tcp` / `rtl_device_index` /
    `rtl_tcp_host` / `rtl_tcp_port` config keys migrate transparently
    to the new shape on first load.
  * Native rtl_tcp client implemented end-to-end in Rust (no Soapy
    on the wire) at src/sdr/rtltcp.rs: 12-byte dongle-info header
    parse, 5-byte BE command frames, blocking CU8 read loop reusing
    the same callback the SoapySDR path uses.
  * Settings modal redesign: 4-tab layout (Connection / Gain /
    Display / Recording) with a transport picker, radio device list,
    configurable preset slot count, and a transport-aware
    connection-string display.
  * Top-bar SDR chip now reflects the active transport instead of
    the cached local driver.
  * 1080p-friendly default dock layout. The top bar wraps to a
    second line on narrow windows so panel toggles stay reachable.

